What is PLC?
PLC (programmable logic controller) is a industrial device and it is a rugged computer used in industry which is used control the industrial process .
it reads input signals from sensors or switches, runs programmed logic, and controls output devices like motors or valves in real time.

PLC programming launguages are standardised undrer the IEC 61131-3.
 IEC->International Electrotechnical Commission ->  global organization that publishes international standards for electrical, electronic, and related technologies
  -> which they ensures safety , productivity ,reliablity and vendor neutral can able to communicate diffrent plc across different vendors.

the IEC 61131 is the IEC standardised for the plc programmings .

PLC programming languages are standardized under IEC 61131-3 and the types of core programming languages  are 
Ladder Diagram (LD) ->  A graphical language modeled after electrical relay circuits using rungs, contacts, and coils
Function Block Diagram (FBD) ->  A graphical language that connects reusable blocks with inputs and outputs.
Sequential Function Charts (SFC) ->  A graphical flowchart-style language using steps, transitions, and branches.
Structured Text (ST),-> A high-level, text-based language similar to Pascal or C. It handles complex math, loops, arrays, and data processing.
and Instruction List (IL)-> A low-level, assembly-like text language. rarely used nowadays.

types of plc?
1.Compact / Nano / Micro PLCs -> they are compact and small . they are all in one with  "combining power supply, CPU, and fixed built-in I/O (20-40 points).all are combined "
->they are used in Standalone machines, packaging units, conveyors, HVAC, and small pumping stations.
2.Modular PLCs -> Separate CPU, power supply, and snap-on I/O modules . you can customise and expand the modules. they are used in ->Mid-to-large production lines,
automotive assembly, and material handling systems.
3.Rack-Mounted PLCs -> Heavy-duty modular systems plugged into a high-speed backplane Supports thousands of I/O points, redundant CPUs, and fast data buses. they are fastest 
and high speed processing . they are used in -> Large process plants, oil and gas, power generation, and chemical manufacturing.
4.-> Safety PLCs -> used in Emergency stops, light curtains, robotic work cells, and high-risk press machinery.
5.-> Soft PLCs / PC-Based Control -> PLC runtime software running on an industrial PC (IPC) or edge device, combining deterministic control with IT/cloud connectivity. they 
are used in -> Smart factories (Industry 4.0), machine vision, high-speed motion control, and data-heavy analytics.




Types of symbols in  Ladder Diagram (LD)

Contacts & Coils
    | | -> Normally Open Contact (NO) - True when bit = 1 - Start button, sensor
    |/| -> Normally Closed Contact (NC) - True when bit = 0 - Stop button, safety
    |P| -> Rising Edge Contact - True for one scan on 0->1 - One-shot
    |N| -> Falling Edge Contact - True for one scan on 1->0 - Detect release
    ( ) -> Coil - Turns bit ON while rung is true - Motor, lamp, flag
    (/) -> Negated Coil - Turns bit ON when rung is false - Inverted output
    (S) -> Set Coil (Latch) - Forces bit ON and holds it - Memory / retain
    (R) -> Reset Coil (Unlatch) - Forces bit OFF - Clear memory
Timers & Counters
Instruction	Full Form	Simple Meaning	Example
TON	Timer On-Delay	->Wait before turning ON	Motor starts after 5 seconds
TOF	Timer Off-Delay	->Wait before turning OFF	Fan runs 5 seconds after motor stops
TP	Pulse Timer	    ->Turn ON for a fixed time	Spray runs for 3 seconds
CTU	Count Up	      ->Count from low to high	Count 10 bottles
CTD	Count Down	     ->Count from high to low	Count 10 bottles remaining
CTUD	Count Up/Down	  ->Count both up and down	Count cars entering and leaving a parking lot
Comparison & Data / Math
    > >= < <= = <> -> Comparison blocks - Compare two values - Thresholds, limits
    MOV -> Move - Copy value - Transfer data
    ADD / SUB / MUL / DIV -> Math - Arithmetic operations - Calculations
